    <div class="tw-move-text" data-reveal>
      <p class="tw-eyebrow">Why the voice</p>
      <h2 class="tw-h2">Every word said — and every one <em>swallowed.</em></h2>
      <p class="tw-p">
        Your voice has been with you since your first cry — every joy, every word
        said, and every one swallowed. When a feeling has nowhere to go, it doesn’t
        disappear. It settles into the body as tension, ache, grief, or a low static
        you’ve long stopped noticing.
      </p>
      <p class="tw-p">
        The voice is the most direct way back to all of it. Not to perform anything.
        To meet what’s there, give it sound, and let it be heard.
      </p>
      <p class="tw-p"><strong>Over twelve weeks, you learn how.</strong></p>
